<section class="process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The request lifecycle</p>
    <h2 id="process-title">A proxy that can learn—without skipping review.</h2>
    <p>Each request is isolated in a child process. A missing capability can produce a candidate implementation, but shipping remains a Git workflow.</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="process-track">
    <li>
      <span class="step-number">01</span>
      <strong>Route</strong>
      <p>Match a forward or reverse route against explicit tenant policy.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-number">02</span>
      <strong>Fork</strong>
      <p>Connect the request and response inside a bounded child workload.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-number">03</span>
      <strong>Generate</strong>
      <p>Ask an approved agent bridge for a narrowly scoped candidate.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-number">04</span>
      <strong>Evaluate</strong>
      <p>Run contracts and policy checks; status 200–302 is only one signal.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="step-number">05</span>
      <strong>Propose</strong>
      <p>Push a feature branch and draft PR with provenance and purpose.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
